    {
      "id": "2110946421243318583",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-16T04:10:20.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-16 12:10:20",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "Tesla now runs half of America’s public DC fast chargers with over 40,000 ports, while the $7.5B federal NEVI program had opened just 384 by April 2025.\n\nOne company built the backbone of the national network with its own capital while the government spent billions and produced a rounding error. \n\nPrivate industry is still outpacing the mandate, and that gap isn’t narrowing anytime soon.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "Rothmus",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1427434033290661891/hLTTZ5lt_200x200.jpg",
