            "height": 900,
            "type": "photo",
            "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUr0lE6XcAA7CJx.jpg?name=small",
            "width": 1600
          }
        ],
        "name": "Rothmus 🏴",
        "text": "Tesla now runs half of America’s public DC fast chargers with over 40,000 ports, while the $7.5B federal NEVI program had opened just 384 by April 2025.\n\nOne company built the backbone of the national network with its own capital while the government spent billions and produced a rounding error. \n\nPrivate industry is still outpacing the mandate, and that gap isn’t narrowing anytime soon.",
